 61NI    59CO(7LI,ANG)                 2019SA04                  ENSDF    202006
 61NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=20-Jan-2020$                    
 61NI c  Dataset adapted from compilation by Jun Chen (NSCL, MSU), Jan 24, 2019,
 61NI2c  for the XUNDL database. Several revisions made in the present dataset. 
 61NI c  2019Sa04: E({+7}Li)=22-24 MeV beam from the Pelletron-LINAC Facility   
 61NI2c  TIFR-Mumbai. Target was 5.2 mg/cm{+2} mono-isotopic {+59}Co on a 4     
 61NI3c  mg/cm{+2} Ta foil. The |g rays were detected with the an array of 11   
 61NI4c  Compton-suppressed Clover HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,
 61NI5c  |g|g(ADO), |g|g(DCO), |g|g(lin pol). Deduced high-spin levels, J|p,    
 61NI6c  multipolarities, branching ratios. Comparisons with                    
 61NI7c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 61NI cG $DCO(D) is for gate |DJ=1, dipole transition and DCO(Q) for gate on    
 61NI2cG |DJ=2, quadrupole. Expected DCO(D)=0.59 {I1} for a |DJ=1,              
 61NI3cG dipole and 0.95 {I1} for |DJ=2, quadrupole; and DCO(Q)=0.96 {I2} and   
 61NI4cG 1.74 {I1}, respectively (2019Sa04)                                     
 61NI cG $Expected R{-ADO} ratios are 1.24 {I2} for |DJ=2, quadrupole           
 61NI2cG transitions and 0.81 {I2} for |DJ=1, dipole transitions (2019Sa04).    
 61NI cG $POL=polarization asymmetry. Expected values are positive for electric 
 61NI2cG transitions and negative for magnetic transitions (2019Sa04).          
 61NI cG $P{-S}=polarization sensitivity, which considers dependence of         
 61NI2cG polarization asymmetry on the gamma-ray energy, as defined in 2019Sa04 
 61NI cG RI$From 2019Sa04. Evaluator notes that branching ratios in several     
 61NI2cG cases disagree with previous fairly precise data from (n,|g) and       
 61NI3cG (|a,n|g), as noted in comments. There seems no discussion by           
 61NI4cG 2019Sa04 about these disagreements.                                    
 61NI cG M$From 2019Sa04 based on measured |g|g(|q)(DCO), |g|g(|q)(ADO) and     
 61NI2cG |g|g(lin pol) data                                                     
 61NI cG M(a)$2019Sa04 assign M1+E2 from their |g|g(|q) data and, in some       
 61NI2cG cases also from |g|g(lin pol), where POL value overlaps zero.          
 61NI3cG Evaluator assigns D+Q in such cases based on experimental data,        
 61NI4cG with the understanding that it is likely to be M1+E2, but not          
 61NI5cG confirmed yet.                                                         
 61NI cG M(b)$2019Sa04 assign E2 from their |g|g(|q) data and, in some          
 61NI2cG cases also from |g|g(lin pol), where POL value overlaps zero.          
 61NI3cG Evaluator assigns Q in such cases based on experimental data,          
 61NI4cG with the understanding that it is likely to be E2, but not             
 61NI5cG confirmed yet.                                                         
 61NI cG M(c)$2019Sa04 assign M1 from their |g|g(|q) data and, in some          
 61NI2cG cases also from |g|g(lin pol), where POL value overlaps zero.          
 61NI3cG Evaluator assigns D in such cases based on experimental data           
 61NI cG M(d)$2019Sa04 assign E1+M2 from their |g|g(|q) data and, in some       
 61NI2cG cases also from |g|g(lin pol), where POL value overlaps zero.          
 61NI3cG Evaluator assigns D+Q in such cases based on experimental data         
 61NI cG M(e)$2019Sa04 assign E1 from their |g|g(|q) data and, in some          
 61NI2cG cases also from |g|g(lin pol), where POL value overlaps zero.          
 61NI3cG Evaluator assigns D in such cases based on experimental data           
 61NI cL E$Deduced from least-squares fit to E|g data                           
 61NI cL J$As given in 2019Sa04, based on measured |g|g(DCO), |g|g(ADO) and     
 61NI2cL |g(lin pol), and previously known assignments for low-lying states.    
